  "details": "Please expand the AV Debug console to compensate for the ever increasing amounts of layers and AV parameters.\nWith 256bits of parameters rolling out and dynamics allowing for non-sync'd variables, the list feels far too \"small\" and hard to navigate when trying to debug avatars ingame. The pagedown/up scrolling is difficult to do in vr, as for some reason pressing said keys in XSoverlay doesnt work.\nIn Desktop it'd be neat if you could just scroll the console with your mousewheel or clickdrag through the list.\nIn VR, there's no reason to limit the panel size, as it currently is- Instead just having the list get \"infinitely\" longer the more layers/parameters it contains would make it easier to read at a glance. Effectively you'd end up with a really long panel if you have a lot of parameters. If not, then again, simply being able to click and drag or scroll with the stick while holding the panel would be enough to speed things up.\nCheers <3",
